
sloctl get slos

Get SLOs by name or available filters. Names can be supplied as arguments or
read from standard input. Without names, all matching SLOs are returned. Use --
project to select a project or --all-projects to search all projects. By
default, all matching SLOs are returned. Use --limit and --offset to request a
page.

Usage

  sloctl get slos [name...] [flags]

Aliases

slos, slo, SLO, SLOs

Flags

 Flag                      | Description
---------------------------|----------------------------------------------------
 -A, --all-projects        | Select resources across all projects.
 -l, --label stringArray   | Filter by label. Repeat the flag or separate
                           | labels with commas, for example:
                           | team=platform,env=prod.
     --limit int           | Maximum number of SLOs to return (1-1000).
     --offset int          | Number of SLOs to skip (requires --limit).
 -p, --project string      | Select resources from this project instead of the
                           | configured default project.
 -s, --service stringArray | Filter SLOs by service name. Repeat to select
                           | multiple services.

Global Flags

 Flag                 | Description
----------------------|---------------------------------------------------------
     --config string  | Path to config.toml. If unset, use
                      | SLOCTL_CONFIG_FILE_PATH or the platform default.
 -c, --context string | Use this context instead of the configured default for
                      | the selected command.
 -h, --help           | Help for sloctl.
 -q, --jq string      | Filter or transform command output using a jq
                      | expression.
     --no-config-file | For API authentication, use SLOCTL_CLIENT_ID and
                      | SLOCTL_CLIENT_SECRET without reading or creating
                      | config.toml. Configuration commands still access the
                      | file.
 -o, --output format  | Output format: yaml, json, csv. (default yaml)
